In a series of discussions, James explored improvements to the Arachne stock growth prediction algorithm and its broader evaluation system. The conversation covered the need for an enhanced backtesting infrastructure to validate algorithm performance, emphasizing the importance of maintaining a common interface for all algorithms' predictions. Specific adjustments were suggested, including settling forecasts by actual trading observations and refining the skill calculation to focus on empirical scores rather than densities. The predictive distribution approach was affirmed, with recommendations on improving diagnostics through better coverage plots and error analysis. Additionally, plans for an Arachne V1.12 version were proposed, suggesting a shift toward an explainable ensemble of specialists to enhance prediction accuracy and interpretability.
